  "question": {
    "text": "If $(2,3,5)$ is one end of a diameter of the sphere $x^2+y^2+z^2-6 x-12 y-2 z+20=0$, then the coordinates of the other end of the diameter are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YRvN1",
      "text": "\n$(4,9,-3)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "uPv5I",
      "text": "\n$(4,-3,3)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IbtKY",
      "text": "\n$(4,3,5)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VfI39",
      "text": "\n$(4,3,-3)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Coordinates of centre $(3,6,1)$\nLet the coordinates of the other end of diameter are $(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma)$ \nthen $\\frac{\\alpha+2}{2}=3, \\frac{\\beta+3}{2}=6, \\frac{\\gamma+5}{2}=1$\nHence $\\alpha=4, \\beta=9$ and $\\gamma=-3$.",
    "image": null
  },
